From: Tianyu9748 <54686548+Tianyu9748@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 18:34:09 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 22/26] [Diffusion] Rotary embedding: out= writes the rotation
 into a given tensor (restored KV in place)

apply_rotary_embedding (Triton), both torch fallbacks (CPU/MPS, NPU),
_apply_rotary_emb and causal_wan_rotate_key take an optional out= of x's
shape and device: x's dtype, or bfloat16/float16 for a float32 x; a
unit-stride last dimension; no memory shared with x (the kernel is
autotuned, and autotuning re-runs it on the same pointers). The result is
written there and returned, e.g. straight into a KV cache slot; invalid
outputs raise and write nothing. The kernel and its arithmetic are
unchanged: the store casts to the output's element type, so the bits are
those of the returned tensor without out= (for a narrower out: of that
tensor .to(out.dtype), rounded once, as RAVEN's rotate(k).type_as(v)).
Without out= every call is unchanged. New unit test
multimodal_gen/test/unit/test_rotary_out.py (8 tests).

Step 5c's F6 proposal ("RoPE into the cache slots"), applied unchanged:
ReelCache/artifacts/sglang_integration/benchmarks/restore_e2e/results/rope_out/
proposal_F6/sglang_rope_out.patch (sha256 0b28372c840128e7...; 5c's
evidence: unit tests 8/8 CPU and 8/8 A100 job 4430990, microbench A100
4430956). ReelCache side: Step 11's overlay release v7 (freeze F6), whose
DenseInstall rotates restored keys straight into their slots when
causal_rotate_key takes out=. Branch reelcache-f6 from reelcache-overlap-proto
7168db64e3 (the F5.x pin, unchanged).

